  "summary": {
   "status": "complete",
   "text": "In an April 16, 2026 official statement as NSA director, Joshua Rudd said AI research and development is constant and helps stay ahead of foreign adversaries also developing AI tools. In February 2026 statements, Rudd agreed that China is aggressively seeking advanced AI chips to accelerate AI-enhanced weapons and said advanced AI chips are foundational to AI superiority and national security. Rudd also said delays of weeks or months in procuring the latest AI chips would impair Department innovation and lethality by stalling integration of cutting-edge AI into weapon systems and cyber threat detection platforms. In April 2026, Rudd said AI is central to the transformation of warfare and that he continues to invest in AI and automation to accelerate delivery of insights and outcomes.",
   "sids": [
    "s1",
    "s4",
    "s5",
    "s3",
    "s6",
    "s7"
   ],
   "sentences": [
